# juri-portfolio

Personal investment portfolio tracker (Argentina-focused: IOL, dólar, crypto).

## Stack

- React 19 + TypeScript + Vite 7 + Tailwind CSS 4
- TanStack React Query for async data
- Vitest + React Testing Library for tests
- Firebase (auth + Firestore sync), Express proxy for IOL API

## Structure

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `src/components/` | UI components (default export) |
| `src/hooks/` | Custom hooks (named export) |
| `src/utils/` | Pure logic + `.test.ts` siblings |
| `src/services/` | API clients and caches |
| `src/types/index.ts` | Shared interfaces |
| `src/config/constants.ts` | `ASSET_TYPES`, `API_ENDPOINTS`, etc. |

## Commands

- `npm run dev:full` — backend + frontend (required for IOL quotes)
- `npm run typecheck` — TypeScript check
- `npm run test:run` — run tests once
- `npm run lint` — ESLint

## Conventions

- UI text and user-facing messages in **Spanish**
- Minimize scope: match existing patterns, no drive-by refactors
- Persist user data via `useLocalStorageState(key, initial, user?.uid)`
- Use `ASSET_TYPES` for asset discrimination; branch to specialized cards (`PlazoFijoCard`, `EfectivoCard`, etc.)
- Env vars: `import.meta.env.VITE_*` only; never commit `.env`
- IOL calls go through the Express backend proxy, not directly from the browser
